          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is a lean protein source: Fruity Cereal has 110 calories, 1 g of fat and 1 g of sugar for 23 g of protein, per the label. The trade-offs are sucralose and acesulfame potassium, gums and flavorings, and no third-party certification. For most healthy adults it is a reasonable way to add protein. People with kidney disease or other medical conditions should check with a doctor first."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Alani protein powder have lactose?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is low in lactose but not lactose-free. The protein is whey isolate and hydrolysate, which are filtered to remove most lactose, and the DigeZyme blend includes lactase to help break down what remains. The label still lists milk as an allergen. People with mild intolerance often do fine; anyone with a milk allergy should avoid it completely."
